    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, returning **409 Conflict**, following the existing duplicate-telephone/household patterns in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`, carrying the offending normalized email.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception that returns a 409 via the shared `conflict(...)` helper, with an `errors: [\"email\"]` array and a matching detail message.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 normalizes the email once (existing `EmailNormalizer`, which lower-cases via `Locale.ROOT`), then calls a new `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` that reuses the existing `existingOwnerMatches` helper to compare against every other owner's lower-cased email. A `null` (omitted) email is never rejected, and owners without an email are ignored.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).",
